<article class="env-definition" id="06DL">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06DL">Definition <span data-tag="06DL">66.23.2</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be an algebraic space over $S$. Let $x \in |X|$. We say that $X$ is <em>geometrically unibranch at $x$</em> if the equivalent conditions of Lemma <a href="/tag/06DK" data-tag="06DK">66.23.1</a> hold. We say that $X$ is <em>geometrically unibranch</em> if $X$ is geometrically unibranch at every $x \in |X|$. </p>
</article>